1. Copyright

VectorLume – source code, program files, documentation, icons and graphics – is protected by
copyright. All rights remain with the author unless these terms expressly permit otherwise. The fact
that the source code is publicly visible does not make this project open-source software; no
open-source licence is granted.

2. Permitted use

The program versions published by the author (installer and portable package) may be downloaded,
installed and used free of charge for private and commercial purposes (freeware).

Files and workpieces you create with VectorLume are yours; the author claims no rights in them.

3. Not permitted

Beyond the use permitted under section 2, you may not, without the author's prior consent (text
form, e.g. e-mail, suffices):

   a) reproduce, modify or translate (including compile) the source code, program files or content
      in whole or in part, incorporate them into other software or works, or run your own instances
      of them;
   b) distribute, publish, sell or rent out the project or parts of it, or pass it off as your own
      work;
   c) remove or alter copyright, licence or trademark notices.

Linking to the repository or the official download page is expressly permitted. Uses permitted by
law (in particular sections 44a et seq., 69d and 69e of the German Copyright Act) and viewing and
forking the repository on GitHub under the GitHub Terms of Service remain unaffected.

4. Third-party components

VectorLume uses third-party libraries and fonts (including egui, usvg, lopdf, image, serialport,
nokhwa and the Hershey single-line fonts). They are listed with their licence texts in the file
THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.html, which accompanies every program version and is linked in the About
dialog. They are governed exclusively by their own licences; these terms do not restrict the rights
granted by those licences.

5. Liability and warranty

The software is provided free of charge. The author is therefore liable only for intent and gross
negligence and for fraudulently concealed defects (sections 521, 523, 524 German Civil Code).
Liability under the German Product Liability Act and any other mandatory statutory liability remain
unaffected.

No warranty is given that VectorLume works without errors or is fit for a particular purpose. There
is no entitlement to bug fixes, updates or support. Back up your data regularly.

In particular, it is not warranted that VectorLume works as expected with a particular laser
machine, firmware or material.

6. Laser safety

VectorLume controls laser machines. Laser radiation can severely injure eyes and skin, ignite
material and start fires; fumes can be harmful; a laser head that runs into an obstacle or beyond
its travel range can damage the machine. Errors in settings, files, firmware or the program can
cause unexpected movements or unexpected laser output. You alone are responsible for safe operation.
In particular:

   – never leave the machine running unattended and keep a fire extinguisher at hand;
   – wear laser safety goggles suitable for the wavelength and use extraction or ventilation;
   – only process suitable materials (e.g. no PVC);
   – check every job with the preview and the frame function before starting, and make sure the
     laser head can move freely;
   – follow the manufacturer's instructions and safety notes and the applicable regulations.

7. Trademarks

LightBurn is a trademark of LightBurn Software, LLC. VectorLume is an independent program and is not
affiliated with LightBurn Software; the name is used only to identify the file format (.lbrn2). All
other product and company names mentioned are trademarks of their respective owners.

8. Final provisions

These terms are governed by German law. Mandatory consumer protection provisions of the country of
your habitual residence remain unaffected. If a provision is invalid, the remaining provisions
remain valid. Contact (e.g. for consent under section 3): https://github.com/Lemm1988
